{
  "manufacturer": "DriSteem",
  "manufacturer_slug": "dristeem",
  "model": "Vapor-logic 5 humidifier controller (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "vapor-logic-5",
  "short_model": "Vapor-logic 5",
  "aliases": [
    "Vapor-logic version 5",
    "VL5",
    "Vapor-logic5"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Air handler humidifier (steam humidifier controller)",
  "applies_to": "DriSteem humidifiers with the earlier Vapor-logic version 5 controller, per IOM form VL5-IOM-0914.",
  "summary": "Vapor-logic 5 is the previous-generation DriSteem humidifier controller (electric, GTS gas, XT electrode, STS steam-to-steam and high-pressure systems). Modbus RTU is standard. Its point list is close to Vapor-logic 6 but not identical: input registers for humidity, dew point, demand and output, holding registers for run mode, set points, fieldbus demand and PID, discrete inputs that also report the fill and drain valves, and coils for every alarm and message.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 99,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Points are printed as IR-1 / 30001, HR-1 / 40001, DI-1 / 10001 and coil DV-1 / 1. These are one-based Modicon numbers: subtract one for the wire address (30001 -> input register 0, coil 1 -> coil 0)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "Vapor-logic version 5",
  "source": {
    "title": "Vapor-logic Version 5 Installation and Operation Manual",
    "doc_number": "VL5-IOM-0914 (Part No. 890000-721 Rev B)",
    "revision_date": "2014-09",
    "url": "https://d2tsmyh31fn7w8.cloudfront.net/public-documents/docs/historical-literature/vl5-iom.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 34 (Table 30-1 communications setup), pp. 71-78 (Table 71-1 interoperability variables)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The PDF sits on the CloudFront host that holds DriSteem public documents (historical-literature folder); the document is the DriSteem IOM.",
    "Note 1 of the table states 16-bit input and holding registers and single-bit discrete inputs and coils; its stated ranges (IR1-IR11, HR1-HR10, DI1-DI9, DV1-DV50) are narrower than the rows actually listed, and all listed rows are included.",
    "No scale is printed, so values are whole numbers in the units shown, except Water_until_ADS / Water_until_service, which the table gives in units of 100 lbs or 100 kg.",
    "Units follow the controller's I-P or SI setting. Temperatures are typed INT16 because their ranges go below zero; signedness is not stated.",
    "The set points HR-2 to HR-4 are marked Write in this version (they are RW in Vapor-logic 6).",
    "The description column prints 'Reserved' beside coils DV-1 / DV-2.",
    "Several numbers carry different meanings on GTS, XT, STS and high-pressure (HPS) systems; both meanings are given.",
    "Serial framing (parity, data and stop bits) is not stated in the manual."
  ],
